    STAS-299: pin the one place allowed to read a timeout sentence
    
    The review asked that classification of a stalled boot live at the boot
    boundary and nowhere downstream. Deleting the message leg at the answer
    sites made that the design; this pins it. The pool's lock-expiry sentence
    arrives as a rejected boot rather than an expired budget, so the typed
    wrap in getStore's catch is the only reader it can have now - and the
    neighbouring case, a lock failure that names no expired budget, is the
    pair that makes the assertion mean something rather than merely pass.

diff --git a/packages/cli/src/__tests__/extension-store-boot-transience.test.ts b/packages/cli/src/__tests__/extension-store-boot-transience.test.ts
